# OsanaKami IDE Studio -- build artefacts and workspace-local state.
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored: examples/ and its hello.yarn / sample.json fixtures.
# The fixtures are part of the project, and tools/e2e.py and langs/selftest.mjs
# run them.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# build output (Makefile: BIN = build/infantgod.exe, OBJDIR = build/obj)
#
# build-iaqs/ is the version store's CMake tree and test temp (tools/build-iaqs.ps1):
# objects, CMake caches and iaqs.exe, none of which are source.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
build/
build-iaqs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# workspace-local state (the board document lives at <root>/.infantgod/board.json)
#
# The board is where you put things, so it is project state.  Ignoring all of
# .infantgod/ keeps each clone's layout private; a fork that wants layouts reviewed
# in pull requests should drop the next line and keep board.json instead.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.infantgod/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# C objects and binaries
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.o
*.obj
*.exe
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.dll
*.lib
*.a
*.dSYM/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python (tools/ is standard-library-only, but Python still writes these)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*.pyd
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node: the shell itself still has zero runtime dependencies, but the window
# wrapper (electron/) brings npm in for the first time, so node_modules/ and
# the packager's output are ignored here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# signing material.
#
# The identity tools/make_cert.ps1 creates lives outside the checkout, in
# %USERPROFILE%\.infantgod, so these lines should never match anything.  They
# are here for the case where someone exports a key "just for a second" into the
# tree: a private key that reaches a commit has to be rotated, and the commit
# history keeps it forever.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.pfx
*.p12
*.pw
*.key
*.cer
*.crt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# editors and IDEs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.suo
*.user
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS droppings
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
